IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tasap-dates`
IMPORT `tasap-survival`

-- Administration and Probate Act 1935 (Tas), s 27 -- worked cases for the survival questions.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- (c) State of Tasmania. Quoted under CC BY 4.0 from an unofficial plain-text copy (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Based on
-- material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names for the facts and the answers used below`

`14 Dec 2005` MEANS `the calendar date` 14 12 2005
`15 Dec 2005` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 12 2005
`17 Dec 2006` MEANS `the calendar date` 17 12 2006
`18 Dec 2006` MEANS `the calendar date` 18 12 2006
`1 Jan 2020` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 2020
`31 May 2023` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 5 2023
`1 Jun 2023` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 6 2023
`31 Aug 2023` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 8 2023
`27 Feb 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 27 2 2024
`28 Feb 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 2 2024
`29 Feb 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 29 2 2024
`15 Mar 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 3 2024
`1 Jun 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 6 2024
`1 Jul 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 7 2024
`15 Aug 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 8 2024
`31 Aug 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 8 2024
`1 Sep 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 9 2024
`15 Sep 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 9 2024
`1 Oct 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 10 2024
`1 Dec 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 12 2024
`15 Feb 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 2 2025
`16 Feb 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 16 2 2025
`28 Feb 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 2 2025
`1 Mar 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2025
`1 Jun 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 6 2025
`2 Jun 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 2 6 2025
`7 Nov 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 7 11 2026

`HAD` MEANS `a claim the dead person had against someone else (it would benefit the estate)`
`AGAINST` MEANS `a claim someone has against the dead person (it would be brought against the estate)`

`SURVIVES FOR` MEANS `yes: it survives for the benefit of the dead person's estate (s 27(1)(b)); the personal representative may bring or continue it, with damages limited by s 27(3)`
`SURVIVES AGAINST` MEANS `yes: it survives against the dead person's estate (s 27(1)(a)); proceedings in tort must meet s 27(5)`
`SURVIVES BY 27(4)` MEANS `yes: s 27(4) deems it to have existed against the person before they died, so it survives against the estate (s 27(1)(a), s 27(4)); proceedings in tort must meet s 27(5)`
`BEFORE 2006` MEANS `not answered: the death was before 18 December 2006, when the former s 27(2) (not deposited) was omitted; that text may have excepted this kind of claim (NOTHING-kind)`
`NO CAUSE AT DEATH` MEANS `s 27 does not reach it: no cause of action existed at the death (NOTHING-kind)`

`MESO` MEANS `mesothelioma`
`ASBESTOSIS` MEANS `asbestosis`
`OTHER LUNG` MEANS `another pathological condition of the lung, pleura or peritoneum`
`NO DUST CONDITION` MEANS `another condition, or no condition of this kind`

`DUST NOT NEEDED` MEANS `the rule is not needed: the death was not caused by the act or omission the claim is about, so s 27(3)(c) does not take those damages out`
`DUST YES` MEANS `yes: the estate may recover damages for pain and suffering, bodily or mental harm and curtailment of expectation of life (s 27(3A))`
`NOT DUST-RELATED` MEANS `no: the condition is not a dust-related condition (s 27(3B), the text's no); s 27(3)(c)(ii) takes those damages out`
`DUST IF FAILS` MEANS `no: s 27(3A) needs the person to have commenced a proceeding on the claim before they died, and to have died as a result of the condition or with it a contributing factor (the text's no: its "if" fails); s 27(3)(c)(ii) takes those damages out`
`ENDED BEFORE 2005` MEANS `no: judgment had been given in the proceeding, or it had been settled or withdrawn, before 15 December 2005 (s 27(3C), the text's no); s 27(3)(c)(ii) takes those damages out`

`TORT` MEANS `a claim in tort (negligence, trespass, nuisance and so on)`
`FATAL ACCIDENTS` MEANS `a claim under the Fatal Accidents Act 1934`
`CONTRACT` MEANS `another kind of claim (contract, debt and so on)`

`PENDING` MEANS `yes: proceedings against the person were pending when they died (s 27(5)(a))`
`TAKEN IN TIME` MEANS `yes: you took proceedings in time, not later than 6 months after the grant of probate or letters of administration, or the extended time a judge allowed (s 27(5)(b))`
`STILL IN TIME` MEANS `still in time: you have not yet taken proceedings, and the last day (6 months after the grant, or the extended time allowed) has not passed (s 27(5)(b))`
`NOT BEGUN` MEANS `still in time: probate or letters of administration have not been granted, so the 6 months has not begun (s 27(5)(b))`
`OUT OF TIME` MEANS `out of time (s 27(5)(b), the text's no): a judge may still extend the 6 months, on an application made even after it has expired (s 27(6))`
`AROSE TOO EARLY` MEANS `no: the cause of action arose earlier than 12 months before the death, and no proceedings were pending when the person died (s 27(5), the text's no)`
`NO 27(5) CONDITION` MEANS `s 27(5) sets no condition: the claim is not in tort or under the Fatal Accidents Act 1934 (NOTHING-kind); the ordinary limitation law still applies`

`RC YES` MEANS `yes: the personal representative may distrain on the land for the arrears, as the dead person could have (s 27(7))`
`RC NO` MEANS `no: the land is no longer in the possession of the person liable to pay the rent-charge or of those deriving title under them (s 27(7), the text's no)`
`RC NOT REACHED` MEANS `s 27(7) does not reach it: the arrears were not due or accruing to the dead person in their lifetime (NOTHING-kind)`
`RENT YES` MEANS `yes: the lease or tenancy has not ended, and the personal representative may distrain for the arrears as the dead person could have (s 27(8))`
`RENT YES AFTER END` MEANS `yes: the lease or tenancy has ended, but the distress is within 6 months after it ended and you are still in possession (s 27(8)(a) and (b))`
`RENT NO` MEANS `no: after the lease or tenancy ended, distress is allowed only within 6 months after it ended and while the tenant remains in possession (s 27(8), the text's no)`
`RENT NOT REACHED` MEANS `s 27(8) does not reach it: the arrears were not due or accruing to the dead person (NOTHING-kind)`

§ `s 27(1) and (4) -- does the claim survive`

-- The day before and the day of 18 December 2006 (fork F1).
#ASSERT `s 27(1) -- does the claim survive the death` `17 Dec 2006` `HAD` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `BEFORE 2006`
#ASSERT `s 27(1) -- does the claim survive the death` `18 Dec 2006` `HAD` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `SURVIVES FOR`
#ASSERT `s 27(1) -- does the claim survive the death` `17 Dec 2006` `AGAINST` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `BEFORE 2006`
-- A claim the dead person had, which had arisen: survives for the estate (s 27(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `s 27(1) -- does the claim survive the death` `1 Jun 2024` `HAD` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `SURVIVES FOR`
-- A claim against the dead person, which had arisen: survives against the estate (s 27(1)(a)).
#ASSERT `s 27(1) -- does the claim survive the death` `1 Jun 2024` `AGAINST` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `SURVIVES AGAINST`
-- Damage suffered only at or after the wrongdoer's death: s 27(4) deems the cause of action to have existed.
#ASSERT `s 27(1) -- does the claim survive the death` `1 Jun 2024` `AGAINST` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `SURVIVES BY 27(4)`
#ASSERT `s 27(1) -- does the claim survive the death` `1 Jun 2024` `AGAINST` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NO CAUSE AT DEATH`
-- s 27(4) speaks only of a cause of action "against" a person: it does not help a claim the dead person had.
#ASSERT `s 27(1) -- does the claim survive the death` `1 Jun 2024` `HAD` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `NO CAUSE AT DEATH`

§ `s 27(3A) to (3C) -- the dust-related condition rule`

#ASSERT `s 27(3A) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` FALSE `MESO` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS `DUST NOT NEEDED`
-- A named disease: no need to show it is attributable to dust.
#ASSERT `s 27(3A) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE `MESO` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS `DUST YES`
#ASSERT `s 27(3A) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE `ASBESTOSIS` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS `DUST YES`
#ASSERT `s 27(3A) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE `silicosis` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS `DUST YES`
-- s 27(3B)(b): another lung, pleura or peritoneum condition counts only if attributable to dust.
#ASSERT `s 27(3A) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE `OTHER LUNG` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS `DUST YES`
#ASSERT `s 27(3A) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE `OTHER LUNG` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS `NOT DUST-RELATED`
-- A condition of another organ is not dust-related even if attributable to dust.
#ASSERT `s 27(3A) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE `NO DUST CONDITION` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS `NOT DUST-RELATED`
-- s 27(3A)(b) and (c), each failing alone.
#ASSERT `s 27(3A) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE `MESO` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS `DUST IF FAILS`
#ASSERT `s 27(3A) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE `MESO` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS `DUST IF FAILS`
-- s 27(3C): ended the day before 15 December 2005, and on that day (fork F4).
#ASSERT `s 27(3A) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE `MESO` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `14 Dec 2005` EQUALS `ENDED BEFORE 2005`
#ASSERT `s 27(3A) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE `MESO` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `15 Dec 2005` EQUALS `DUST YES`

§ `s 27(3) -- the damages the estate recovers`

-- Facts: damages up to death 50,000; non-economic 80,000; earnings after death 300,000; other loss from the death
-- 20,000; funeral 10,000; exemplary 25,000.
-- Death caused by the wrong, no dust-related condition: 50,000 + 10,000 funeral = 60,000.
#ASSERT `s 27(3) -- how much can the estate recover` TRUE FALSE 0 50000 80000 300000 20000 10000 25000 `NO DUST CONDITION` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS 60000
-- The same with mesothelioma and s 27(3A) met: 60,000 + 80,000 = 140,000.
#ASSERT `s 27(3) -- how much can the estate recover` TRUE FALSE 0 50000 80000 300000 20000 10000 25000 `MESO` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS 140000
-- Mesothelioma but the proceeding was not commenced before death: 60,000.
#ASSERT `s 27(3) -- how much can the estate recover` TRUE FALSE 0 50000 80000 300000 20000 10000 25000 `MESO` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS 60000
-- Mesothelioma, proceeding settled on 14 December 2005: 60,000.
#ASSERT `s 27(3) -- how much can the estate recover` TRUE FALSE 0 50000 80000 300000 20000 10000 25000 `MESO` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `14 Dec 2005` EQUALS 60000
-- Death not caused by the wrong: everything but exemplary damages: 50,000 + 80,000 + 300,000 + 20,000 + 10,000 = 460,000.
#ASSERT `s 27(3) -- how much can the estate recover` FALSE FALSE 0 50000 80000 300000 20000 10000 25000 `NO DUST CONDITION` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS 460000
-- Breach of promise to marry: only the damage to the estate (5,000), or none.
#ASSERT `s 27(3) -- how much can the estate recover` FALSE TRUE 5000 50000 80000 300000 20000 10000 25000 `NO DUST CONDITION` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `s 27(3) -- how much can the estate recover` FALSE TRUE 0 50000 80000 300000 20000 10000 25000 `NO DUST CONDITION` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS 0

§ `s 27(5) -- the last day to take proceedings against the estate`

#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- by when must I take proceedings against the estate` FALSE `15 Mar 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- by when must I take proceedings against the estate` TRUE `15 Mar 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS JUST `15 Sep 2024`
-- 31 August plus 6 months: no 31 February, so the last day of February (fork F7); in a leap year 29 February.
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- by when must I take proceedings against the estate` TRUE `31 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS JUST `28 Feb 2025`
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- by when must I take proceedings against the estate` TRUE `31 Aug 2023` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS JUST `29 Feb 2024`
-- An extension to a later day; an "extension" ending sooner does not shorten the 6 months (fork F8).
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- by when must I take proceedings against the estate` TRUE `15 Mar 2024` TRUE `1 Dec 2024` EQUALS JUST `1 Dec 2024`
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- by when must I take proceedings against the estate` TRUE `15 Mar 2024` TRUE `1 Sep 2024` EQUALS JUST `15 Sep 2024`

§ `s 27(5) -- can I take proceedings against the estate`

-- Death 1 June 2024; grant 15 August 2024; the last day 15 February 2025.
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `CONTRACT` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` `1 Jun 2024` TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `NO 27(5) CONDITION`
-- Pending at the death: maintainable however early the cause of action arose.
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` TRUE `1 Jan 2020` `1 Jun 2024` TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `PENDING`
-- The last day, and the day after.
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `FATAL ACCIDENTS` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `15 Feb 2025` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `TAKEN IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `16 Feb 2025` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `FATAL ACCIDENTS` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `16 Feb 2025` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
-- Arose the day before 12 months before the death (out, even if taken in time), and exactly 12 months before (in).
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `31 May 2023` `1 Jun 2024` TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `1 Sep 2024` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `AROSE TOO EARLY`
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `1 Sep 2024` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `TAKEN IN TIME`
-- Death on 28 February 2025: 12 months before is 28 February 2024; 29 and 28 February 2024 are in, 27 February out.
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `28 Feb 2024` `28 Feb 2025` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` `1 Mar 2025` EQUALS `NOT BEGUN`
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `29 Feb 2024` `28 Feb 2025` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` `1 Mar 2025` EQUALS `NOT BEGUN`
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `27 Feb 2024` `28 Feb 2025` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` `1 Mar 2025` EQUALS `AROSE TOO EARLY`
-- No grant yet but proceedings already taken: in time (fork F9).
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `1 Jul 2024` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `TAKEN IN TIME`
-- Taken before the grant, then the grant: day 0, in time (fork F9).
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `1 Jul 2024` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `TAKEN IN TIME`
-- Not yet taken: today is the last day (still in time), and the day after (out of time).
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` `15 Feb 2025` EQUALS `STILL IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` `16 Feb 2025` EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
-- An extension to 1 June 2025: its last day in time, the day after out.
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` TRUE `15 Aug 2024` TRUE `1 Jun 2025` TRUE `1 Jun 2025` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `TAKEN IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` TRUE `15 Aug 2024` TRUE `1 Jun 2025` TRUE `2 Jun 2025` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`

§ `s 27(5) -- the regulative rule alone`

-- Grant to last day: 15 August 2024 to 15 February 2025 is 16 + 30 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 31 + 15 = 184 days.
#ASSERT `the days from` `15 Aug 2024` `to` `15 Feb 2025` EQUALS 184
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- taking proceedings on this day is in time` 184 0
#ASSERT `s 27(5) -- taking proceedings on this day is in time` 184 184
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 27(5) -- taking proceedings on this day is in time` 184 185))

§ `s 27(7) and (8) -- distress by the personal representative`

#ASSERT `s 27(7) -- can the executor distrain for the rent-charge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `RC YES`
#ASSERT `s 27(7) -- can the executor distrain for the rent-charge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `RC NO`
#ASSERT `s 27(7) -- can the executor distrain for the rent-charge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `RC NOT REACHED`

#ASSERT `s 27(8) -- can the executor distrain for the rent` FALSE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` `1 Oct 2024` TRUE EQUALS `RENT NOT REACHED`
#ASSERT `s 27(8) -- can the executor distrain for the rent` TRUE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` `1 Oct 2024` TRUE EQUALS `RENT YES`
-- Ended 31 August 2024: 6 months after is 28 February 2025 (in), 1 March 2025 (out).
#ASSERT `s 27(8) -- can the executor distrain for the rent` TRUE TRUE `31 Aug 2024` `28 Feb 2025` TRUE EQUALS `RENT YES AFTER END`
#ASSERT `s 27(8) -- can the executor distrain for the rent` TRUE TRUE `31 Aug 2024` `1 Mar 2025` TRUE EQUALS `RENT NO`
-- Within the 6 months but the tenant has left.
#ASSERT `s 27(8) -- can the executor distrain for the rent` TRUE TRUE `31 Aug 2024` `1 Oct 2024` FALSE EQUALS `RENT NO`
